Abstract
FitTrack is an AI-powered fitness and wellness platform that helps users track workouts, meals and body progress in one place, and receive personalized guidance generated by Generative AI. Many people struggle to stay consistent with fitness goals because their data is scattered across notebooks and apps, generic plans ignore personal goals, and reviewing progress is manual and time-consuming. FitTrack addresses these problems by letting users log activity and automatically generate workout plans, diet plans, progress insights and motivational tips.
The backend is developed with Node.js and Express.js following a RESTful architecture, with MongoDB and Mongoose ODM for data storage. Security is ensured through JWT-based authentication, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and password hashing with bcryptjs. The system integrates the Google Gemini AI API to dynamically generate personalized fitness content from the profile and activity data supplied by the user. The modular MVC design keeps the platform scalable, maintainable and open to future enhancements.
Keywords: Generative AI, Google Gemini, Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, JWT, RBAC, REST API, Fitness Tracking, Workout Plan, Diet Plan.
1. Introduction
Staying fit requires regular exercise, balanced nutrition and consistent monitoring of progress. Busy students and professionals rarely have time to research suitable routines, count calories and analyse their own results. Fitness data is often spread across notebooks, spreadsheets and several apps.
Generative AI models can understand user data and produce tailored recommendations. FitTrack uses this capability through the Google Gemini API, wrapped in a secure and modular backend, to give users a single platform for AI-assisted fitness management.
1.1 Scenario-Based Case Study
Arun is a college student who wants to lose weight and build stamina while managing a heavy class schedule. He follows random online routines, forgets what he exercised last week, and cannot tell whether his diet supports his goal. Writing a weekly plan, calculating calories and reviewing progress by hand is repetitive and leads to inconsistent results. With FitTrack, Arun enters his profile and goal, logs his workouts and meals, and instantly receives a personalized plan and progress feedback.
2. Problem Statement
Users face the following challenges while trying to stay fit:
Lack of personalized workout plans based on goal, fitness level and available time.
Difficulty planning balanced meals that match calorie and nutrition targets.
Workout, meal and body-measurement records scattered across multiple apps and notebooks.
Manual effort needed to analyse progress and identify what is working.
Loss of motivation due to lack of feedback and regular guidance.
No centralized and secure platform to store AI-generated fitness resources.
3. Objectives
To build a secure, centralized platform where users can store fitness profiles, workout logs and meal logs.
To generate personalized workout plans automatically using the Google Gemini API.
To generate diet plans based on goals, food preferences and calorie needs.
To provide AI progress insights and motivational tips from the logged data.
To protect user data using JWT authentication, RBAC and bcryptjs password hashing.
To follow a modular MVC architecture that supports future enhancements.
4. Scope of the Project
The project covers the design and development of a RESTful backend that handles user registration and login, fitness profile management, workout and meal logging, AI content generation (workout plans, diet plans, progress insights, tips), storage and retrieval of generated content, and administrative management of users. A React.js frontend consumes these APIs. The platform is intended for students, beginners and general fitness enthusiasts, and can be extended with wearable-device integration, progress charts and multilingual support. It provides general fitness guidance and is not a substitute for advice from a medical professional.
