8.1 Key Relationships
User - Profile: One-to-One: each user has one fitness profile.
User - Workout Log: One-to-Many: a user can record many workouts.
User - Meal Log: One-to-Many: a user can record many meals.
User - Workout Plan / Diet Plan: One-to-Many: a user can generate multiple plans as goals change.
User - Insight: One-to-Many: insights are generated for different time periods.
User - AI Resources: One-to-Many: every generated resource is linked to the user who created it.
9. Modules and Key Features
Secure User Authentication: JWT-based login with passwords encrypted using bcryptjs.
Profile Management: Store age, height, weight, goal and fitness level used as AI input.
Workout and Meal Logging: Add, view, update and delete daily activity and food records.
AI Workout Plan Generation: Personalized weekly routines produced with the Gemini API.
AI Diet Plan Generation: Meal plans matched to calorie targets and food preferences.
AI Progress Insights: Summary of recent activity with suggestions for improvement.
Role-Based Access Control: Different privileges for Users and Administrators.
MongoDB Data Storage: Persistent storage of users, logs and generated resources.
9.1 Roles and Responsibilities
User: Registers, logs in securely, maintains a profile, logs workouts and meals, and generates and reviews plans and insights.
Administrator: Manages user accounts, monitors application and AI service usage, reviews system logs and resolves user issues.
10. User Flow
The user registers or logs in to the application.
After successful JWT authentication, the user is redirected to the dashboard.
The user completes the fitness profile (age, height, weight, goal, level).
The user logs workouts and meals, or selects an AI feature: workout plan, diet plan or progress insights.
The backend sends the profile and log data to the Google Gemini API and receives the generated output.
The result is displayed to the user and saved in MongoDB for future reference.
The user can view and manage profile details and earlier logs and plans from the dashboard.
